{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Goal\n\nFix forward after CL 2626: restore the direct-engine legacy-route `--filter-local-ids` post-filter that CL 2626 removed, while keeping the legitimate removals of top-level `rebar reconcile`, direct `--mode reconcile-check`, and stale `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` status diagnostics.\n\nWhy restore the flag: the active live Jira DC CI harness needs verbatim raw-key matching for inbound creates whose Jira key has no binding yet. Primary `--only` resolves before the differ and cannot express that case.\n\nPreserve `_ref_lock.py` pause sentinel `gated_mode == \"reconcile-check\"` and keep `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK` in `mode.py`/`_ORDERED`/`MODE_CAPS` because `_advisory_lock._mode_blocks` decodes the persisted sentinel through `Mode.from_str`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Keep removed: top-level `rebar reconcile` registration/help/parser, direct `--mode reconcile-check`, `_run_reconcile_check`, `reconcile_check.py`, its JSON writer/reader, and `reconcile_diagnostics` schema/type/MCP fields.\n- Restore: `--filter-local-ids` argparse support on the direct-engine legacy route in `request.py`, parsed into `ReconcileRequest.filter_local_ids`, and handed through `__main__.py` to `run_pass` for post-filtering.\n- Reject `--filter-local-ids` on primary `preview`/`sync`; primary `--only`/`--except` remains pre-scoping selection, not a replacement for the post-filter.\n- Revert the external live-DC harness helper to emit `python -m rebar_reconciler --mode <mode> --filter-local-ids <ids>` and keep comments/READMEs accurate about post-filter scoping.\n- Clean live source comments that named deleted `reconcile_check.py`; leave immutable ADR historical references alone.\n\n## Design decisions\n\n1. Replacement remains distributed: `bridge preview` for live proposed changes, `bridge fsck --output json` for offline binding/orphan audits, and `bridge status --json` for operational state without stale reconcile-check diagnostics.\n2. `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK` stays as load-bearing persisted pause vocabulary, but direct `--mode reconcile-check` rejects before operational work.\n3. `--filter-local-ids` is restored engine-only and legacy-route-only because it is a post-filter: it seeds targets with tokens verbatim and matches mutation target/provenance after the full differ. This preserves live-DC inbound-create scoping for raw Jira keys with no existing binding.\n4. Follow-up `f8c4-ac9b-42c5-4bb0` owns any deeper selection/filter redesign.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_mode.py` proves the retained enum/order/caps support the pause sentinel.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py` proves `--mode reconcile-check` rejects and `_run_reconcile_check` is not dispatched.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge.py tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py` proves the retained runner profile invokes `bridge preview`.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_heldout.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_relocated_store.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic_heldout.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_model_schema_drift_heldout.py` proves BridgeStatus no longer exposes `reconcile_diagnostics`.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/scripts/test_jira_pressure_test_preflight.py tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge.py tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py` proves the pressure probes preflight before mutation and the reconciler bridge profiles route through canonical bridge commands.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock_ref_backend.py` proves pause docs still preserve `gated_mode == \"reconcile-check\"`.\n- [x] NEW `tests/interfaces/facades/test_filter_local_ids_engine_restore_82bb_heldout.py` and NEW `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_filter.py::TestFilterLocalIdsLegacyRoute` prove the engine-only `--filter-local-ids` legacy-route post-filter parses/hands off raw Jira keys and primary `preview`/`sync` reject the flag.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconcile_cli_state_removal_82bb_heldout.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_filter_local_ids_engine_restore_82bb_heldout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_filter.py::TestFilterLocalIdsLegacyRoute` proves top-level `rebar reconcile` and `--mode reconcile-check` remain removed while the post-filter is restored.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` passes.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck` passes.\n- [x] `env GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=4 GIT_CONFIG_KEY_3=safe.bareRepository GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_3=all PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test` passes, deselecting only confirmed pre-existing host artifact `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin_and_keeps_refs_isolated` if needed.\n\n## Testing\n\nHeld-out oracles: `tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconcile_cli_state_removal_82bb_heldout.py`, NEW `tests/interfaces/facades/test_filter_local_ids_engine_restore_82bb_heldout.py`, NEW `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_filter.py::TestFilterLocalIdsLegacyRoute`, `tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py`, `tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge.py`, and `tests/scripts/test_jira_pressure_test_preflight.py`. The new restoration oracle must be RED against the post-CL-2626 tree and GREEN after restoring the flag; mutation teeth must show removing the restored flag kills it.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- `_lib_ops.py` / `_mcp_reads.py` Python/MCP `rebar.reconcile(mode=...)` removal was completed by c195.\n- Do not change `_ref_lock.py` pause sentinel bytes/schema.\n- Do not change canonical preview/sync/fsck/status semantics except removing stale status diagnostics.\n- Do not force any ticket operation."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788564776984791001,"uuid":"65c439f1-7fae-4406-8583-f03e93a4b400"}